  "responsibility_boundary": "Phase 7 separates seven production Python facades into cohesive Skill CLI, Agent run, Skill registry, Workspace CLI, Project Tour, Action Loop, and Storage Episode owners while preserving their stable public modules.",
  "cohesion_rationale": "The twelve new owner modules are the minimum cumulative responsibility set needed to remove the seven Phase 7 monoliths. Storage Episode commands live in the storage domain rather than inflating the CLI aggregate, and each remaining helper owns an independently changing command, transport, persistence, or native-operation boundary.",
  "rejected_split_alternatives": [
    "Keeping any of the seven responsibility groups in its original facade would retain an over-1000-line handwritten production module.",
    "Splitting individual commands or functions into smaller arbitrary files would increase indirection without creating independent ownership.",
    "Moving domain behavior solely to satisfy a metric, changing public imports, or relaxing the aggregate structure baseline would hide debt instead of reducing it."
  ],
